{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/424700-crossover-question-amkhat-totemed-skinthief","id":424700,"title":"Crossover Question: Amkhat-Totemed Skinthief","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T17:50:45-08:00","id":424700,"title":"Crossover Question: Amkhat-Totemed Skinthief","content":"Anyway, one of my applications for this huge crossover chronicle is, as the title suggests, a skinthief whose totem is actually an Amkhat, who uses his natural link with intangibility to sneak into places, steal vessels for his Arisen master, and sneak out, relying on raw power to defend himself if need be (which he has a lot of, his totem once being the Greater Amkhat a Shuankshen, in a reckless-presumably-move sent after him after he started to theorize about a predecessor to the proto-Egyptian kingdoms). He's also fairly unique in that while he might lose his mind, he won't lost his intellect-I volunteered a houserule that he instead suffers an increasing loss of control over his self-identity, and the ST amended it to he being prone to frenzy states.<br /> <br /> My question is that, when it comes to it, he's a person with a Sekhem-hungry monster wrapped around his soul. While I have it that he's obsessed with acquiring vessels and memorizing every aspect he can find with his eyes and hands, I want to know any other ideas for how this might affect his personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T17:37:16-08:00","id":427155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/424700-crossover-question-amkhat-totemed-skinthief#post424700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is that, when it comes to it, he's a person with a Sekhem-hungry monster wrapped around his soul. While I have it that he's obsessed with acquiring vessels and memorizing every aspect he can find with his eyes and hands, I want to know any other ideas for how this might affect his personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is a person who has collected a creature, of whom hunger for life equals that of a Kindred Eldar or the Strix, skinned it, and transforms into it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I would have the Amkhat slowly leech Sekhem from the dude over time until he consumes a source, which keeps it off of him for a bit before the hunger takes him over again.<br /> <br /> Devouring those who are fresh with Sekhem (mostly kids and freshly raised Arisen) would also play a part.<br /> <br /> So in short, it's a Mummy's take on the Werewolf myth. Should have the local Uratha packs in a tizzy when reports of a &quot;Wild animal devouring kids!&quot; hits the front page news.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}